From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 20:44:53 -0400
Subject: media: cix: add <linux/string.h> includes + strncpy->strscpy (7.2
 build fix)

Forward-port fix on top of the 7.1 sky1-next port (1/2 + 2/2 in this
series). Not in any upstream sky1-next patch; required to build the
driver against 7.2-rc1 mainline.

Three files in drivers/media/platform/cix/ use string.h primitives but
do not include <linux/string.h>:

  - if/mvx_firmware_v2.c:    uses memcpy(), strscpy()
  - if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c: uses memcpy(), memset()
  - if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c:    uses strncpy()

On 7.1 the compiler happened to pick these up via transitive includes
(likely from <linux/slab.h> in earlier 7.x). In 7.2 the include chain
no longer drags them in, so the build fails with:

  drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c:123:5: error:
    implicit declaration of function 'strncpy'
    [-Werror=implicit-function-declaration]

Add explicit "#include <linux/string.h>" to all three files, and
replace the single strncpy() call in mvx_ext_if_register_device()
with strscpy() (which IS declared in <linux/string.h>). strscpy is
the upstream-recommended replacement for bounded string copies; the
buffer here is the 64-byte video_device.name[], null-terminated by
strscpy after the copy (vdev.name is documented to be a C string, so
that's the correct contract).

Result: drivers/media/platform/cix/amvx.ko builds clean, ~575 KB
unstripped, depends=videobuf2-v4l2,videodev,videobuf2-dma-sg,
videobuf2-common, vermagic=7.2.0-rc1-ncz.
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_firmware_v2.c      | 1 +
 drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c    | 3 ++-
 drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c | 1 +
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_firmware_v2.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_firmware_v2.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_firmware_v2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/mvx_firmware_v2.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/dma-buf.h>
 #include <linux/dma-mapping.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include "fw_v2/mve_protocol_def.h"
 #include "mvx_firmware_cache.h"
 #include "mvx_firmware_priv.h"
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_ext_v4l2.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/err.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/videodev2.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-ctrls.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-device.h>
@@ -120,7 +121,7 @@ int mvx_ext_if_register_device(struct mvx_ext_if *ext,
                 V4L2_CAP_VIDEO_M2M_MPLANE |
                 V4L2_CAP_EXT_PIX_FORMAT |
                 V4L2_CAP_STREAMING;
-    strncpy(ext->vdev.name, name, sizeof(ext->vdev.name));
+    strscpy(ext->vdev.name, name, sizeof(ext->vdev.name));
 
     video_set_drvdata(&ext->vdev, ext);
 
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/if/v4l2/mvx_v4l2_vidioc.c
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/sched.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-ctrls.h>
 #include <media/v4l2-event.h>
